  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759371,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 120 Yen no Haru - 120 Yen Stories (PS2) - Synopsis\n\nExperience a unique and charming collection of interconnected short stories in *120 Yen no Haru*, a delightful anthology game from Neko Neko Soft, originally inspired by a digital novel from a fandisk. This unusual release for the PlayStation 2 presents four distinct narratives, each unfolding across a single season of the year.\n\nDive into the lives of unique male and female characters as they navigate relationships and intriguing situations, all tied together by the enigmatic phrase \"120 Yen.\"  The PS2 version features two original stories alongside those from the original release. Progress through the anthology by completing each seasonal tale, unlocking the next chapter and revealing more about the overarching mystery.\n\n*120 Yen no Haru* offers a refreshing departure from traditional game narratives, delivering bite-sized stories perfect for short play sessions. With its limited playtime and a release price reflecting that, this is a truly special and memorable experience for fans of visual novels and character-driven stories."
    },
